ted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1118554#post1118554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah but did we need such a big chapter when they only appear at the end? When more relevant antagonist are missing updates? No we didnt, but by now i am tired of this argument and people so insecure of their game/taste they feel they must &quot;defend&quot; their game from criticism of any kind in a thread about PERSONAL TASTES and miss the difference between reducing and removing. So i am out of here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Yes we did.<br /> Because a large part about the Idigam chapter is how they create their minions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:23:10-07:00","id":1118606,"title":"","content":"Yes, all 21 pages describing their aptitudes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T06:05:34-07:00","id":1118930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1118554#post1118554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yeah but did we need such a big chapter when they only appear at the end? When more relevant antagonist are missing updates? No we didnt, but by now i am tired of this argument and people so insecure of their game/taste they feel they must &quot;defend&quot; their game from criticism of any kind in a thread about PERSONAL TASTES and miss the difference between reducing and removing. So i am out of here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, it's a thread about personal tastes. Your criticism on the large spotlight on the idigam that could have been given to other interesting antagonists is a legitimate expression of personal taste, and actually a fine point of criticism on the book. That we all know.<br /> <br /> But somehow people stating their own personal tastes on the topic, that at least some of us find it satisfactory or at least necessary that while other antagonists could use some wordcount the book is doing fine on presenting the idigam as it is, is those people being insecure and thus not a legitimate expression of personal taste?<br /> <br /> Call me rude for dragging you back into something you want to check out of, and thus feel free to ignore me, but being called insecure for being active in proposing personal tastes and perspectives that happened to disagree with that of yours isn't exactly a pleasant experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T06:26:14-07:00","id":1118934,"title":"","content":"My view is simple here. New werewolves seems to be stronger and badasser than old (at least on the level with vampires - and I speak here not just about fighting abilities). Hence, they are better.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love it...this makes werewolves truly the scariest thing in the WoD. AS THEY SHOULD BE! </div> </div> </div>Demons and Beasts right now:<br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/zCNhS9Xoubzji/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Also Promethids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 07-21-2017, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","r