milieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not just you. The consensus in my LARP group was that werewolves were the most powerful template in combat, besides maybe mages, given enough exp. And we had a lot of hardcore character optimizers in that group. We did agree though that werewolves needed way more exp to get that good than most other templates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:02:31-07:00","id":1119247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119245#post1119245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not just you. The consensus in my LARP group was that werewolves were the most powerful template in combat, besides maybe mages, given enough exp. And we had a lot of hardcore character optimizers in that group. We did agree though that werewolves needed way more exp to get that good than most other templates.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I agree. They were very exp inefficient, which was their core problem. Other than that? They had really high strength, ability to regenerate, along with Savage Rending for scene length aggavated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T14:59:12-07:00","id":1119340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119235#post1119235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunted all those before.</div> </div> </div> </div> Really? Some descriptions of the hunts? Tactics, template, anything?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T15:04:10-07:00","id":1119341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119340#post1119340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Really? Some descriptions of the hunts? Tactics, template, anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a modified Spirit Whispers facet that allowed me to command the spirit of objects, which allowed us to get into an unchained's bolthole, the least place which he considered we'd we waiting to ambush him. The fight didn't lasted 1 turn.<br /> <br /> The Beast ran afoul of us when it's presence near to our locus attracted an undue amount of fear spirits which we convinced to try and devour it for tasty essence.<br /> <br /> The Promethean was lit on fire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T17:49:58-07:00","id":1119370,"title":"","content":"I've found Beasts to be not that imposing on their own. They have nice abilities but they can't really refuel well in combat. The one in the Night Horrors book cowing an entire community of werewolves wasn't believable at all but I get the feeling some writers don't know much about Forsaken, by things like that and repeated use of Apocalypse terms and systems. This isn't a dig, I don't believe everyone should have to read every book possible just to write, especially if working for another line and there's a lot of settings out there.<br /> <br /> And if you want <i>scary</i>, you go for a Werewolf of the Lodge of the Screaming Moon, with the Gift of the Screaming Moon. Or the Fangs of Mara, if they ever get a nice second edition update. Certain Nosferatu bloodlines take Nightmare to another level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":".  Think original wording came across as too offensive or insulting. 07-23-2017, 04:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T18:25:00-07:00","id":1119377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119341#post1119341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had a modified Spirit Whispers facet that allowed me to command the spirit of objects, which allowed us to get into an unchained's bolthole, the least place which he considered we'd we waiting to ambush him. The fight didn't lasted 1 turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could have turned out badly if the Demon had Self-Destruct on the Bolthole. And 4-Minutes Ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T20:32:03-07:00","id":1119390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119370#post1119370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found Beasts to be not that imposing on their own. They have nice abilities but they can't really refuel well in combat. The one in the Night Horrors book cowing an entire community of werewolves wasn't believable at all but I get the feeling some writers don't know much about Forsaken, by things like that and repeated use of Apocalypse terms and systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only such reference I can find in Conquering Heroes is talking about an Insatiable intimidating an unspecified number of Forsaken into serving him, the Insatiable in question also has the Atavism that allows him to make a contested roll to immediately inflict Beaten Down after a successful attack, and one of the primary advantages of Atavisms is that they don't need Satiety to do their basic functions normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-22-2017, 11:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T21:27:24-07:00","id":1119399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119390#post1119390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only such reference I can find in Conquering Heroes is talking about an Insatiable intimidating an unspecified number of Forsaken into serving him</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Insatiable in question also has the Atavism that allows him to make a contested roll to immediately inflict Beaten Down after a successful attack, and one of the primary advantages of Atavisms is that they don't need Satiety to do their basic functions normally. </div> </div> </div>The Atavism you're referring to only has that ability during Low Satiety.<br /> <br /> And of course, 'Most Uratha \u2014 along with other creatures that don\u2019t have a problem killing people \u2014 can ignore surrender without penalty and don\u2019t get Beaten Down.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T21:42:04-07:00","id":1119403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119399#post1119399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Atavism you're referring to only has that ability during Low Satiety.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the opposite of an obstacle to its deployment for a being that's near-explicitly using an ability that costs Satiety in a context where Satiety expenditure is to be expected \u2014 just because The Authority statted as a major power player in [insert city here] has Satiety 6 doesn't mean the character has been locked at that level in perpetuity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And of course, 'Most Uratha \u2014 along with other creatures that don\u2019t have a problem killing people \u2014 can ignore surrender without penalty and don\u2019t get Beaten Down.' </div> </div> </div>In the context of normal combat, yes. When figuring out how different supernatural powers interact with different supernatural beings, respecting the fiction comes first, <i>especially</i> in the context of a fictional background event where the werewolves in question just had their leader reduced to ash.<br /> <br /> All of which is secondary to the fact that the Insatiables are not Beasts in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T22:10:01-07:00","id":1119412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119403#post1119403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the opposite of an obstacle to its deployment for a being that's near-explicitly using an ability that costs Satiety in a context where Satiety expenditure is to be expected \u2014 just because The Authority statted as a major power player in [insert city here] has Satiety 6 doesn't mean the character has been locked at that level in perpetuity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just clarifying, it's not the standard ability of the Atavism, and not always available. But none of that matters because the power wasn't what caused the servitude in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the context of normal combat, yes. When figuring out how different supernatural powers interact with different supernatural beings, respecting the fiction comes first, <i>especially</i> in the context of a fictional background event where the werewolves in question just had their leader reduced to ash. </div> </div> </div>Why bring up Looming Presence to begin with, then. It's at least implied by the fiction that it wasn't used. Some werewolves were 'beaten senseless,' the others were told to serve, and they and at least some future werewolves were so afraid that they serve him too. Even with a Satiety Expenditure the Beaten Down isn't an area affect ability.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All of which is secondary to the fact that the Insatiables are not Beasts in the first place. </div> </div> </div>There you go, right. He's not a Beast, he's an Insatiable<br /> <br /> I stated it wasn't believable. You're not making this any more believable. It tilts more comic than Chronicles. This is usually where you usually be dismissive of my views and imply that I don't understand things the way you do, if history is anything to go by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T22:41:45-07:00","id":1119420,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, the Authority can deal aggravated damage with just his fists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T22:49:55-07:00","id":1119422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119420#post1119420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, the Authority can deal aggravated damage with just his fists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with a cost of 1 Aggravated damage to himself.<br /> <br /> But werewolves can do it with just their teeth without a similar cost.<br /> <br /> I like the book, I've already said so in the thread when it came out. I just believe this part of it is unbelievable in the context of Chronicles of Darkness as it's been depicted in other books. Offhand, I'd say it was inspired by the Daredevil series on Netflix, specifically the Kingpin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-23-2017, 02:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T06:04:26-07:00","id":1119478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"http