functions normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all those Forsaken took punches whilst in Hishu. Try to inflict that condition on a Gauru.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I had my older brother burned to a crisp I wouldn't surrender, I'd Kuruth the shit out of there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 07-24-2017, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T05:37:49-07:00","id":1119849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119480#post1119480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So all those Forsaken took punches whilst in Hishu. Try to inflict that condition on a Gauru.<br /> <br /> I mean, if I had my older brother burned to a crisp I wouldn't surrender, I'd Kuruth the shit out of there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Btw, Malus, did you played crossever in 1st and 2nd edition? If yes, which one do you prefer?<br /> P.S. it is not about other splats as antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T07:06:37-07:00","id":1119868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1118002#post1118002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For example a 5 dot fetish weapons given as an example: sap wp or health (quantity not determined) and has 8s again/rote quality. <br /> <br /> It is a mighty weapon but not one that warranties messing with a rank 5 spirit. Is too little for such a big cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean. We can disagree about how receiving both 8 again and rote quality on an action isn't worth it, but you ignored the other example which states that a 5 dot fetish can perform actions that explicitly break the rules, i.e. using defense against mental attacks. The endless possibilities i find with 3 dot fetishes modifying facets just pales in comparison to what I can do with a 5 dot fetish. They are most certainly worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:23:04-07:00","id":1119880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119849#post1119849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, Malus, did you played crossever in 1st and 2nd edition? If yes, which one do you prefer?<br /> P.S. it is not about other splats as antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both. 2e got easier ways to one-shot people or several people. And the games tended to turn in pvp because different factions provoked each other by messing with the other's resources.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119868#post1119868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean. We can disagree about how receiving both 8 again and rote quality on an action isn't worth it, but you ignored the other example which states that a 5 dot fetish can perform actions that explicitly break the rules, i.e. using defense against mental attacks. The endless possibilities i find with 3 dot fetishes modifying facets just pales in comparison to what I can do with a 5 dot fetish. They are most certainly worth it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having both 8 again and rote action amounts to basically doubling your base dice pool. IE, if you roll 12 dice with 8 again and rote action, you're potentially rolling 24 dice, or an average of 8 successes. Indeed, that's boring. Stuff an abyssal-corrupted spirit into a fetish and walk around unraveling/corrupting magic left and right. There you go, now you have an antagonist/mystery for your mage game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 07-24-2017, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T08:30:57-07:00","id":1119886,"title":"","content":"Ok, it's a bit dull, but you can't deny the effect is <i>powerful</i>. That's what makes it 5 dot tier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T13:16:07-07:00","id":1120038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119880#post1119880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having both 8 again and rote action amounts to basically doubling your base dice pool. IE, if you roll 12 dice with 8 again and rote action, you're potentially rolling 24 dice, or an average of 8 successes. Indeed, that's boring. Stuff an abyssal-corrupted spirit into a fetish and walk around unraveling/corrupting magic left and right. There you go, now you have an antagonist/mystery for your mage game.</div> </div> </div> </div>At minimum you are doubling your dice pool most likely going above that with extra successes being rerolled. It may be boring but it is undeniably powerful and fits a 5 dot fetish well in my opinion. Regardless my point was even if you don't like that, they do so much more then 8 again and rote qualities. They are extremely powerful even based off of what is given to us in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-25T02:23:13-07:00","id":1120273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117739-differences-in-w-tf-1e-vs-2e?p=1119412#post1119412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is usually where you usually be dismissive of my views and imply that I don't understand things the way you do, if history is anything to go by.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This wasn't necessary. It reads as a dare/provocation, please avoid statements like this in the future, thanks.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}